where the other copy has a different observation x' and so runs a different node than mine. That means my intervention doesn't reach its output, which it instead gets from its own distribution, and the situation resembles the red/blue coordination setup.\n\nWorking through the payoffs, submitting comes out ahead by 2 − q whatever the other copy does, so defecting holds up across every q. I'm also weighing whether the inputs being symmetric would make the two copies effectively the same node, but the essay ties the node to the observation, so the different names and leads still separate them. Under that reading both copies land on submit, and I'll go with it.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm treating this under A-FDT, where the other copy has a different observation x' and so runs a different node than mine. That means my intervention doesn't reach its output, which it instead gets from its own distribution, and the situation resembles the red/blue coordination setup.\n\nWorking through the payoffs, submitting comes out ahead by 2 − q whatever the other copy does, so defecting holds up across every q. I'm also weighing whether the inputs being symmetric would make the two copies effectively the same node, but the essay ties the node to the observation, so the different names and leads still separate them. Under that reading both copies land on submit, and I'll go with it.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9278,"completion_tokens":991,"total_tokens":10269,"cost":0.056932,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.056932,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.037112,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01982},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":452,"image_tokens":0,"audio